  "notes": "### New\n\n- A new Settings screen with categories for General, Updates, Accounts, Privacy, and Help and about\n- Sign in with more than one Samsung account and see which TVs use each one\n- Install a saved copy of Tvaro IPTV Player on your TV when there's no internet\n- A QR code and download button make it easy to get the Android app from your computer\n- On Android phones, choose which update notifications you get right in the app\n- Privacy policy and Terms of use links in Help and about\n\n### Improved\n\n- A sharper, cleaner Tvaro logo on app icons and screens\n- Android phones now get a simpler top bar, full-screen language and theme choices, and bottom sheets\n- Clear messages when your Wi-Fi or internet connection is down, and installs pick up again when it's back\n- When a TV already has Tvaro IPTV Player from another device or account, the app explains it, shows your account and offers a way forward\n- A dropdown for choosing your language, ready for more languages\n\n### Fixed\n\n- On Android 17, finding TVs and adding one by IP address work again once you allow Nearby devices\n- A saved copy of Tvaro IPTV Player no longer replaces a newer version on your TV\n- On Android phones, the System theme now applies right away\n- Signing in again after you cancel or close the browser now works\n- Settings rows no longer sit under the navigation bar on Android phones\n- The theme choice no longer cuts off \"System\"\n- Messages no longer cover the screen title on Android phones",
